{title: Glorious Things of Thee Are Spoken}
{artist: John Newton / Franz Joseph Haydn}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: F}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: glorious-things-of-thee-are-spoken.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Glorious_Things_of_Thee_Are_Spoken-Austria_Haydn-Austrian_Hymn)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Glorious things [C7]of thee [F]are [C7]spo[F]ken,
[F]Zion, [C7]ci[F]ty [Gm]of [G7]our [C]God!
[Dm]He, whose [C7]word cannot [F]be [C7]bro[F]ken,
[Bb]Formed [F]thee [Gm]for [F]His [Gm]own [G7]a[C7]bode.
[C7]On the Rock of Ages founded,
[Am]What can [Dm]shake thy [G7]sure re[C]pose?
[F]With sal[Bb]va[F]tion’s [Bb]walls sur[Dm]round[F]ed,
[C7]Thou may’st smile at all thy [F]foes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]See! the streams [C7]of liv[F]ing [C7]wa[F]ters,
[F]Springing [C7]from [F]e[Gm]ter[G7]nal [C]love;
[Dm]Well supp[C7]ly thy sons [F]and [C7]daugh[F]ters,
[Bb]And [F]all [Gm]fear [F]of [Gm]want [G7]re[C7]move:
[C7]Who can faint while such a river
[Am]Ever [Dm]flows their [G7]thirst t’as[C]suage?
[F]Grace, which [Bb]like [F]the [Bb]Lord, the [Dm]giv[F]er,
[C7]Never fails from age to [F]age.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Round each hab[C7]ita[F]tion [C7]ho[F]vering,
[F]See the [C7]cloud [F]and [Gm]fire [G7]ap[C]pear!
[Dm]For a [C7]glory and [F]a [C7]co[F]vering
[Bb]Show[F]ing [Gm]that [F]the [Gm]Lord [G7]is [C7]near.
[C7]Thus deriving from our banner
[Am]Light by [Dm]night and [G7]shade by [C]day;
[F]Safe they [Bb]feed [F]up[Bb]on the [Dm]man[F]na
[C7]Which He gives them when they [F]pray.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Savior, if [C7]of Zi[F]on’s [C7]ci[F]ty,
[F]I through [C7]grace [F]a [Gm]mem[G7]ber [C]am,
[Dm]Let the [C7]world deride [F]or [C7]pi[F]ty,
[Bb]I [F]will [Gm]glo[F]ry [Gm]in [G7]Thy [C7]name:
[C7]Fading is the worldling’s pleasure,
[Am]All his [Dm]boasted [G7]pomp and [C]show;
[F]Solid [Bb]joys [F]and [Bb]lasting [Dm]trea[F]sure
[C7]None but Zion’s children [F]know.
{end_of_verse}
